    if [file], creates fact, [fact pattern]
    and [fact pattern], names, [predicate]

[predicate], is, open
    if [any level], lets every level state, [fact pattern]
    and [fact pattern], names, [predicate]

[file], breaks, Each predicate has one creator
    if [file], creates, [predicate]
    and [other file], creates, [predicate]
    and [other file], differs from, [file]
    and not [predicate], is, open

a workflow that fakes what the tools returned, adds line, kernel/agent.plain, "command: a fake, returned, file, nowhere"
a workflow that fakes what the tools returned, must break, Each predicate has one creator

a spec that looks for itself, adds line, kernel/human.plain, "kernel/ghost.txt, is, in the folder"
a spec that looks for itself, must break, Each predicate has one creator

a workflow that makes up a result, adds line, kernel/agent.plain, "a comment, broke, The only knowledge is Datalog"
a workflow that makes up a result, must break, Each predicate has one creator

"kernel/engine.go, loads, kernel/human.plain", means in mangle, 'loads("kernel/engine.go", "kernel/human.plain").'
"kernel/human.plain, is, in the folder", means in mangle, in_the_folder("kernel/human.plain").
the knowledge is broken, means in mangle, the_knowledge_is_broken().
there is a problem, means in mangle, there_is_a_problem().
"[any file], is, a used file", means in mangle, a_used_file(AnyFile).
"true, exits with, 0", means in mangle, 'exits_with("true", 0).'
'a change, adds line, notes.plain, "a, is, a note"', means in mangle, 'adds_line("a change", "notes.plain", "a, is, a note").'
"a change, adds line, notes.csv, 1,2", means in mangle, 'adds_line("a change", "notes.csv", "1,2").'
"[file], ends with, [ending]", means in mangle, ":string:ends_with(File, Ending)"
"[command], starts with, [prefix]", means in mangle, ":string:starts_with(Command, Prefix)"
"[file], differs from, [other file]", means in mangle, File != OtherFile
"[time], is before, [other time]", means in mangle, ":lt(Time, OtherTime)"
"[difference], is the difference of, [later], [earlier]", means in mangle, "Difference = fn:minus(Later, Earlier)"
"[difference], is at most, [tolerance]", means in mangle, ":le(Difference, Tolerance)"
"[number], is one more than, [other number]", means in mangle, "Number = fn:plus(OtherNumber, 1)"
"[entity], is the join of, [prefix], [value]", means in mangle, "Entity = fn:string:concat(Prefix, Value)"
'[command], is the join of, "command: find the comments in ", [file]', means in mangle, 'Command = fn:string:concat("command: find the comments in ", File)'

[rule], breaks, Every rule reads back as written
    if [rule], is, read back differently

a rule that reads back differently, adds line, kernel/human.plain, "kernel/engine.go, loads, kernel/extra.plain"
a rule that reads back differently, adds line, kernel/extra.plain, '"zzz", means, nothing'
a rule that reads back differently, must break, Every rule reads back as written
a rule that reads back differently, must explain, '"b55a370302a20713, breaks, Every rule reads back as written", holds because, "b55a370302a20713, is, read back differently"'

kernel, expects, "00021adce41fe7b6, is in the file, kernel/human.plain"
kernel, expects, "00021adce41fe7b6, is on line, 1"

[rule], breaks, No rule is written twice
    if [rule], is on line, [number]
    and [rule], is on line, [other number]
    and [number], differs from, [other number]
[rule], breaks, No rule is written twice
    if [rule], is in the file, [file]
    and [rule], is in the file, [other file]
    and [file], differs from, [other file]
No rule is written twice, is, a warning

a rule written twice, adds line, kernel/human.plain, "true, exits with, 0"
a rule written twice, must break, No rule is written twice
a rule written twice, must answer, true

.plain, means, plain language
.go, means, go
go.mod, means, go module
go.sum, means, go checksums
.sh, means, sh
.csv, means, rows

[file], breaks, The only knowledge is Datalog
    if [file], is, in the folder
    and not [file], is, known
[file], breaks, The only knowledge is Datalog
    if [file], has the comment, [any comment]

a file that is not datalog, adds line, kernel/notes.txt, a note
a file that is not datalog, must break, The only knowledge is Datalog

a comment, adds line, kernel/tools.go, // a note
a comment, must break, The only knowledge is Datalog
a comment, must explain, '"kernel/tools.go, breaks, The only knowledge is Datalog", holds because, "kernel/tools.go, has the comment, // a note"'

[change], is, a change
    if [change], adds line, [any file], [any line]
