    if [fact pattern], names, [predicate]
    and [predicate], is, observed

engine.go, prints, the knowledge
engine.go, prints in, plain language
engine.go, prints to, standard output
the knowledge, shows, [folder] conforms [answer]
the knowledge, shows, [thing] breaks [law]
the knowledge, shows, [change] broke [law]
the knowledge, shows, [change] answered [answer]
the knowledge, shows, [change] explains [explanation]
the knowledge, shows, [text] is a problem
the knowledge, gives reasons for, [thing] breaks [law]

a rule id, is computed as, the first 16 hex digits of the sha256 of the rule lines joined by newlines
a rule name, is computed as, the rule id
a fact id, is computed as, the first 16 hex digits of the sha256 of the fact as one plain line
a derivation id, is computed as, the first 16 hex digits of the sha256 of the fact and the rule id and the reasons as plain lines joined by newlines

the knowledge, is published to, the store
the knowledge, is published only when, true
the store, is the sqlite file, the level store
the certificate, holds, the name of the level being proven
the certificate, holds, the hash of every file engine.go loads or the level is tested with
the certificate, holds, the hash of every file that is part of the machine
the certificate, holds, the answer

the store, has the table, rules
rules, has a row for, every rule
rules, has the column, 1, id, the rule id
rules, has the column, 2, file, the file the rule is in
rules, has the column, 3, line, the number of the line the rule starts on
rules, has the column, 4, text, the rule lines joined by newlines

the store, has the table, facts
facts, has a row for, every fact
facts, has the column, 1, id, the fact id
facts, has the column, 2, text, the fact as one plain line
facts, has the column, 3, origin, the go file that observed the fact and derived for every other fact

the store, has the table, derivations
derivations, has a row for, every way a rule derives a fact
derivations, has the column, 1, id, the derivation id
derivations, has the column, 2, fact_id, the fact id
derivations, has the column, 3, rule, the rule id

the store, has the table, reasons
reasons, has a row for, every reason of every derivation
reasons, has the column, 1, derivation_id, the derivation id
reasons, has the column, 2, position, the number of the condition in the rule
reasons, has the column, 3, reason, the condition with its blanks filled as one plain line

the store, has the table, certificate
certificate, has a row for, every part the certificate holds
certificate, has the column, 1, part, what the certificate holds
certificate, has the column, 2, subject, the file a hash is of and empty otherwise
certificate, has the column, 3, value, the sha256 of the file in hex or the level name or the answer

plain language, is loaded as, rules and facts
rows, is loaded as, a row per line after the first with a cell for each column the first line names
a row name, is computed as, the file name and a colon and the line number
a cell value, is computed as, the cell text read as a plain value
a quoted value, is computed as, a value between double quotes unless it holds a double quote and no single quote and then between single quotes
a quote inside a quoted value, is computed as, the quote the value is between written twice
a part of a line, is computed as, the text between two commas that are each followed by a space
a not condition, is computed as, true when no fact matches it for any value of a blank found nowhere else in its rule

kernel, is tested with, kernel/sample.csv
kernel, expects, "kernel/sample.csv:2, is a row of, kernel/sample.csv"
kernel, expects, "kernel/sample.csv:2, has the cell, name, ann"
kernel, expects, "kernel/sample.csv:2, has the cell, size, 3"
kernel, rules out, "kernel/sample.csv:1, is a row of, kernel/sample.csv"
kernel, rules out, "kernel/sample.csv:2, is, a row without a size"

[row], is, a row without a size
    if [row], is a row of, [any source]
    and not [row], has the cell, size, [any value]
the knowledge, shows, [row] is a row without a size

[fact], breaks, Every expected fact holds
    if [any level], expects, [fact]
    and [fact], is, missing

an expectation that does not hold, adds line, kernel/human.plain, 'kernel, expects, "nothing, is, in the folder"'
an expectation that does not hold, must break, Every expected fact holds
an expectation that does not hold, must answer, false
an expectation that does not hold, must explain, "'""nothing, is, in the folder"", breaks, Every expected fact holds', holds because, '""nothing, is, in the folder"", is, missing'"

[fact], breaks, No ruled out fact holds
    if [any level], rules out, [fact]
    and [fact], is, present

a ruled out fact that holds, adds line, kernel/human.plain, 'kernel, rules out, "kernel/human.plain, is, in the folder"'
a ruled out fact that holds, must break, No ruled out fact holds
a ruled out fact that holds, must answer, false

a missing fact, is computed as, a fact a level expects that the knowledge does not hold without the facts about what is missing or present
a present fact, is computed as, a fact a level rules out that the knowledge holds without the facts about what is missing or present
an agent file, is computed as, agent.plain in a level folder which an agent writes and may rewrite on any run

[other level], breaks, Every level a level builds on is proven
    if [level], builds on, [other level]
    and not [other level], is, proven

a level built on an unproven level, adds line, kernel/human.plain, "kernel, builds on, nowhere"
a level built on an unproven level, must break, Every level a level builds on is proven
a level built on an unproven level, must answer, false

a level, is computed as, a folder next to the kernel folder named by the folder name
the level being proven, is computed as, the level whose folder runme.sh is run in
a level file, is computed as, human.plain or agent.plain in the level folder
a level store, is computed as, the level name followed by .db in the folder that holds the level folders
a loaded level, is computed as, the level being proven and every level a loaded level builds on where a level with no folder loads nothing
a loaded file, is computed as, a level file of a loaded level and every file a level file says engine.go loads
a tested file, is computed as, a file the level being proven is tested with found in its folder and loaded like a file engine.go loads
a file name, is computed as, the path of the file from the folder that holds the level folders
a proven level, is computed as, a loaded level other than the level being proven whose store holds a certificate with the answer true and with the hash of every file it names as that file is now
a certified file, is computed as, a file loaded from the folder of a proven level

[change] adds line [file] [line], is, private to its level
[change] must break [law], is, private to its level
[change] must answer [answer], is, private to its level
[change] must explain [explanation], is, private to its level
[level] expects [fact], is, private to its level
[level] rules out [fact], is, private to its level
a private fact, is computed as, a fact of a private fact pattern which engine.go does not load from a certified file

kernel, lets every level state, [level] lets every level state [fact pattern]
kernel, lets every level state, [go file] loads [file]
kernel, lets every level state, [level] builds on [other level]
kernel, lets every level state, [level] is tested with [file]
kernel, lets every level state, [slot] is a slot name
kernel, lets every level state, [law] is a warning
kernel, lets every level state, [law] is a serious warning
kernel, lets every level state, [thing] breaks [law]
kernel, lets every level state, [knowledge] shows [fact pattern]
kernel, lets every level state, [change] adds line [file] [line]
kernel, lets every level state, [change] must break [law]
kernel, lets every level state, [change] must answer [answer]
kernel, lets every level state, [change] must explain [explanation]
kernel, lets every level state, [level] expects [fact]
kernel, lets every level state, [level] rules out [fact]
